+[[FORCE-PUSHES]]
+FORCE PUSHES
+------------
+
+This build of Git does not force-push. `-f`/`--force` and
+`--force-with-lease` are refused with an error, as is a refspec with a
+leading `+` on the command line. `--force-if-includes` (and
+`push.useForceIfIncludes`) only ever qualified `--force-with-lease`, so
+it has no effect. A `+` refspec
+in `remote.<name>.push`, `--mirror` and `git send-pack --force` no
+longer bypass the fast-forward check, so a non-fast-forward update
+is rejected like any other.
+
+Fast-forward updates, creating refs and deleting refs keep working.
+To replace history you have already published, push it to a new
+branch, or use linkgit:git-revert[1] to undo commits on top of it.
+
